Europe's Common Agricultural Policy the  cap comes under the microscope when  European farm ministers meet on April  22nd the cap helps guaranteed good  living standards for farmers and stable  food suppliers at fair prices for  consumers it also Foster's rural  development and protects the environment  but it accounts for a big slice of the  EU budget at their meeting in Luxembourg  the minister's will be briefed on the  outcome of the first try log  negotiations between the council  parliament and commission since the  council and the Parliament reached  positions on the cap reform package last  month those talks focused on the rules  governing direct payments to farmers the  organisation of markets in agricultural  products rural development support and  the way the cap is financed managed and  monitored if all goes according to plan  do you use Irish presidency hopes to  clinch a comprehensive political Accord  on the reforms by june 30 the Commission  will also present a plan to the  ministers for transitional measures for  next year as the farm package could not  be implemented before 2015 in fisheries  talks the Commission will also unveil an  action plan to reduce the number of  accidental catches of seabirds in  fishing gear these incidents have become  a threat to some bird populations most  involve the use of long line and static  nets  ministers will also hold a public debate  on the first trial of negotiations  between the council Commission and  Parliament on reforming the e use common  fisheries policy the presidency would  like the council to come back on some of  the sensitive issues raised during the  discussions with the other institutions
 

